    <item>Simplify expressions with higher roots</item>
    <item>Use the Product Property to simplify expressions with higher roots</item>
    <item>Use the Quotient Property to simplify expressions with higher roots</item>
    <item>Add and subtract higher roots</item>
  </list>
  <note type="practice" source_type="Be Prepared" title="Be Prepared" number="9.18">
    <paragraph>Before you get started, take this readiness quiz.</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Simplify: $$y^{5}y^{4}$$ . If you missed this problem, review Example 6.18.</paragraph>
  </note>
  <note type="practice" source_type="Be Prepared" title="Be Prepared" number="9.19">
